{
  "wireMagic": "pb3",
  "pens": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wsWinStyles": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wpWinPositions": [ {
  
  } ],
  "events": [ {
    "tStartMs": 80,
    "dDurationMs": 5520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If you want to know if someone really understands \nevolution, just ask them this one weird question."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 5600,
    "dDurationMs": 1760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Why does poop smell bad?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 7360,
    "dDurationMs": 880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Oh."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 8240,
    "dDurationMs": 800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Oh, gosh."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 9040,
    "dDurationMs": 1760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Because it has bacteria in it, I guess?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 10800,
    "dDurationMs": 2080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Microbiome, probably."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 12880,
    "dDurationMs": 800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Trash-"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 13680,
    "dDurationMs": 793,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Yeah, trash from the gut."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 14473,
    "dDurationMs": 647,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "... of the body."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 15120,
    "dDurationMs": 1280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The food we eat?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 16400,
    "dDurationMs": 2000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Because of the chemicals?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 18400,
    "dDurationMs": 2240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Farts don't always smell bad."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 20640,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Yeah. Well, that's a different question \nentirely. Do you think it objectively smells bad?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 25200,
    "dDurationMs": 1360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Yes, I think so."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 26560,
    "dDurationMs": 400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Yes."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 26960,
    "dDurationMs": 2320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "How do you think it smells to flies?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 29280,
    "dDurationMs": 1275,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Like the fly?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 30555,
    "dDurationMs": 805,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Yeah-\nThey like it."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 31360,
    "dDurationMs": 310,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "They love it.\nThey like it, yeah."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 31670,
    "dDurationMs": 810,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "They love it."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 32480,
    "dDurationMs": 1680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Animals love stinky things."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 34160,
    "dDurationMs": 1440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Yeah.\nThey're attracted to it."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 35600,
    "dDurationMs": 3520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Poop smells good to flies because \npoop is full of nutrients."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 39120,
    "dDurationMs": 1920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "They use it as food."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 41040,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But it's also full of bacteria that \ncan be life-threatening to humans."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 45600,
    "dDurationMs": 3120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So the real reason poop \nsmells bad to us is because"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 48720,
    "dDurationMs": 2800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "if anyone ever thought it smelled good,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 51520,
    "dDurationMs": 4160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "they would probably get really sick, \ndie, and not pass on their genes."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 55680,
    "dDurationMs": 2960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "After all, it's about survival of the fittest."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 58640,
    "dDurationMs": 2480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But survival of the fittest what?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 61120,
    "dDurationMs": 1760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I mean, most people think of natural selection  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 62880,
    "dDurationMs": 3120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "as being about the survival of \nthe fittest individual animal."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 66000,
    "dDurationMs": 640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Individual."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 66640,
    "dDurationMs": 640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Individuals."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 67280,
    "dDurationMs": 1600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Individual animal."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 68880,
    "dDurationMs": 1920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Animal. Okay, so it's like an individual."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 70800,
    "dDurationMs": 320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Yeah."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 71120,
    "dDurationMs": 960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Which makes sense."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 72080,
    "dDurationMs": 4240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I mean, individuals best adapted to their \nenvironment have increased odds of survival,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 76320,
    "dDurationMs": 2560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and therefore a higher likelihood \nof passing on their genes."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 78880,
    "dDurationMs": 5680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So it follows that each individual should do \neverything it can to survive and reproduce."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 84560,
    "dDurationMs": 2160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That is, it should be selfish."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 86720,
    "dDurationMs": 3520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But if that's true, then how do you explain this?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 90800,
    "dDurationMs": 4080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Worker bees will sting \npredators to protect the hive,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 94880,
    "dDurationMs": 2640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "even though it might kill them in the process."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 97520,
    "dDurationMs": 2560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Female worker ants are sterile,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 100080,
    "dDurationMs": 1920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "so they can't reproduce,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 102000,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but regardless, they work for the colony \nfor their entire lives until they die."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 106800,
    "dDurationMs": 5440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Monkeys adopt orphans, wolves bring \nmeat to non-hunting members of the pack,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 112240,
    "dDurationMs": 5920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and squirrels can let out alarm calls \nto warn others about nearby predators."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 118160,
    "dDurationMs": 3440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So if natural selection is \nall about selfish individuals,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 121600,
    "dDurationMs": 3600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "why do we observe so much altruism in nature?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 125200,
    "dDurationMs": 3040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The survival is of the species that can adapt."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 128240,
    "dDurationMs": 1200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I think generally the species."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 129440,
    "dDurationMs": 1440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "For the survival of the species."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 130880,
    "dDurationMs": 1495,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So it's the survival of the species."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 132375,
    "dDurationMs": 585,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Okay. Yeah, you're right.\nOkay."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 132960,
    "dDurationMs": 4640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But survival of the fittest species or \nthe fittest group also doesn't work."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 137600,
    "dDurationMs": 4160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I mean, think about what you need \nfor natural selection to occur."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 141760,
    "dDurationMs": 5040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You need something that replicates \nitself many times over, creating copies,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 146800,
    "dDurationMs": 1680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and then you need a pruning process,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 148480,
    "dDurationMs": 5040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "whereby some of those copies get eliminated and \nsome thrive to go on and create more copies."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 153520,
    "dDurationMs": 5760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The problem with groups or species is that \nthey don’t typically make copies of themselves."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 159280,
    "dDurationMs": 2880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So you almost never get copies of groups fighting  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 162160,
    "dDurationMs": 3120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "other copies of groups to \nsee which groups win out."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 165280,
    "dDurationMs": 5280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So if it's not survival of the fittest individual \nand it's not survival of the fittest group,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 170560,
    "dDurationMs": 1360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "then what is it?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 171920,
    "dDurationMs": 3360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Well, to explain that, I want \nto take you on a little journey,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 175280,
    "dDurationMs": 11280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "all the way back to the beginnings of the Earth."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 186560,
    "dDurationMs": 3040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Where we are now, there is nothing."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 189600,
    "dDurationMs": 2640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Well, not really nothing, but nothing interesting."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 192240,
    "dDurationMs": 2880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "There are only simple things, like these blobs."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 195120,
    "dDurationMs": 4080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This one might be a carbon dioxide \nmolecule, or it might be cyanide."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 199200,
    "dDurationMs": 1680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "We don't know for sure what they are,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 200880,
    "dDurationMs": 2880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but we do know that these \ncompounds are very simple."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 203760,
    "dDurationMs": 3680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So for now, they'll just be \nblobs floating around our void."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 207440,
    "dDurationMs": 3840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In fact, much of what we'll encounter \nalong our journey here are just hypotheses."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 211280,
    "dDurationMs": 2400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "A lot of Earth's early history is still a mystery,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 213680,
    "dDurationMs": 1840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "so keep that in mind."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 215520,
    "dDurationMs": 3120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now, every so often, our \nblobs get a surplus of energy,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 218640,
    "dDurationMs": 3680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "maybe from a ray of UV light \nor a nearby hot source."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 222320,
    "dDurationMs": 3920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This is the first major upgrade \nto our void, excess energy,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 226240,
    "dDurationMs": 2800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "as it allows our blobs to \ninteract with each other."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 229040,
    "dDurationMs": 3520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And most of the time, this \ninteraction leads to nothing,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 232560,
    "dDurationMs": 4960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but sometimes these blobs can combine \ninto more complicated compounds. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 237520,
    "dDurationMs": 4240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Here's a simple simulated example, \nwhere we only have four red blobs."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 241760,
    "dDurationMs": 4240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Right now, they are all individual particles, \nbut each time step we move forward,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 246000,
    "dDurationMs": 5000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "let's say there's a 10% chance that all \nfour combine into one red mega-blob."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 251000,
    "dDurationMs": 3560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And now imagine this mega-blob isn't very stable."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 254560,
    "dDurationMs": 1840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "For every time step it's alive,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 256400,
    "dDurationMs": 4960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "it has a 95% chance of falling apart \nback into the four smaller blobs."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 261360,
    "dDurationMs": 5200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If we add more of these red blobs into the mix, \nyou'll notice that they rarely ever come together."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 266560,
    "dDurationMs": 4640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "On average, a mega-blob only \nexists around 10% of the time."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 271200,
    "dDurationMs": 4720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But if we were to reduce the chances of \nthe mega-blobs dissolving to only 1%,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 275920,
    "dDurationMs": 3600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the void would suddenly be filled with them."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 279520,
    "dDurationMs": 3200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This fact hints at an important \nlaw that governs our void,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 282720,
    "dDurationMs": 2320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the law of stability."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 285040,
    "dDurationMs": 6960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Unstable blobs fall apart and \nvanish. Stable ones endure."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 292000,
    "dDurationMs": 2880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now, watch what happens if we \nspeed this up dramatically,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 294880,
    "dDurationMs": 3520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "maybe a couple of years per second, \nmaybe even a couple million."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 298960,
    "dDurationMs": 2960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You can see our blobs keep \ngetting random jolts of energy,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 301920,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "so they combine with others to \nform more complex compounds."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 306480,
    "dDurationMs": 3440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Most attempts fail and fall \napart, but every so often,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 309920,
    "dDurationMs": 1360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "by pure chance,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 311280,
    "dDurationMs": 4480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you get a compound that is more \nstable than the blobs it's made of."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 315760,
    "dDurationMs": 4320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This doesn't happen because the blobs \nwant to build more complex structures."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 320080,
    "dDurationMs": 4720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It's just because these new configurations \nhappen to be more favorable in the environment."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 324800,
    "dDurationMs": 3440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And now when these complicated \ncompounds become abundant enough,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 328240,
    "dDurationMs": 2400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "they too get a chance to combine,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 330640,
    "dDurationMs": 3840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "making our void increasingly complex."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 334480,
    "dDurationMs": 1840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And one day, by accident,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 336320,
    "dDurationMs": 3440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "this causes an extremely unique shape to form,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 339760,
    "dDurationMs": 2240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "one with a special property."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 342000,
    "dDurationMs": 6000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "See, the blobs it's made of just happen to attract \nsimilar blobs from the surrounding environment."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 348000,
    "dDurationMs": 2240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This red blob always attracts green blobs,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 350240,
    "dDurationMs": 2800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and this purple blob always attracts yellow ones,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 353040,
    "dDurationMs": 3360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and piece by piece, all these \nblobs attract their opposites"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 356400,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "until their counterparts suddenly snap \ninto position next to the original shape."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 361200,
    "dDurationMs": 2720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now, this shape goes on to do the same thing."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 363920,
    "dDurationMs": 2000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Its green blobs attract red ones"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 365920,
    "dDurationMs": 5440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and yellow ones attract the purple until \nanother shape yet again snaps into position."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 371360,
    "dDurationMs": 3200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This new shape looks exactly like the original."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 374560,
    "dDurationMs": 4480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "What just happened fully \nspontaneously is replication."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 379040,
    "dDurationMs": 1920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "One shape became two."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 380960,
    "dDurationMs": 4000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This marks the birth of the first replicator."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 384960,
    "dDurationMs": 2640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "We don't know exactly what \nthis replicator looked like."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 387600,
    "dDurationMs": 2400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It might've been a single standalone molecule  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 390000,
    "dDurationMs": 3520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "or a group of molecules that \nworked together to replicate."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 393520,
    "dDurationMs": 1680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "There's a lot of debate on this today,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 395200,
    "dDurationMs": 3680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "so instead, let's represent \nthe replicator as a character."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 398880,
    "dDurationMs": 2000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "How about this one here?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 400880,
    "dDurationMs": 880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Perfect."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 401760,
    "dDurationMs": 5360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Keep in mind it's still just a lifeless \nmolecule, one without any intent or purpose."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 408080,
    "dDurationMs": 4880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now, you might think that the chances for the \nreplicator to form were extremely unlikely,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 412960,
    "dDurationMs": 3760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but in our void, where we have hundreds \nof millions of years to play with,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 416720,
    "dDurationMs": 4080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "what might seem impossible to \nus becomes virtually inevitable."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 420800,
    "dDurationMs": 3920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And the thing is, the replicator \nonly has to arise once."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 424720,
    "dDurationMs": 880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Once it's here,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 425600,
    "dDurationMs": 5920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "it can take the simpler compounds available in the \nenvironment to copy itself at a much faster pace."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 431520,
    "dDurationMs": 1520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And so it does that,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 433040,
    "dDurationMs": 3040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "until it entirely fills our void."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 436080,
    "dDurationMs": 2400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "At least, that's what you'd expect,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 438480,
    "dDurationMs": 3040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but there is a flaw in the process."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 441520,
    "dDurationMs": 2640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "See, during the replicator's conquest of the void,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 444160,
    "dDurationMs": 3600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "one of its copies makes a mistake."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 447760,
    "dDurationMs": 3600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Perhaps a stray ray of UV light hits \nit during the replication process,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 451360,
    "dDurationMs": 4000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "or the replicator uses a building \nblock it wasn't supposed to."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 455360,
    "dDurationMs": 2640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "As a result, what we're left with is a new shape,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 458000,
    "dDurationMs": 2320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "which is slightly different from its parent,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 460320,
    "dDurationMs": 3280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and so its properties might \nbe slightly different too."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 464320,
    "dDurationMs": 1680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This error might be harmful."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 466000,
    "dDurationMs": 2480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "For example, it might make the copy less stable."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 468480,
    "dDurationMs": 3520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It could be beneficial, making \nthe copy better at replicating,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 472000,
    "dDurationMs": 1600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "or it could be neutral,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 473600,
    "dDurationMs": 3040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "not changing the replicator in any meaningful way."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 476640,
    "dDurationMs": 2800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This marks the final milestone in our void,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 479440,
    "dDurationMs": 1040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "mutation."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 480480,
    "dDurationMs": 3280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Many species of replicators now occupy the void,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 483760,
    "dDurationMs": 3280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and what they do is they replicate themselves."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 487040,
    "dDurationMs": 3520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The problem is they all need \nthe same limited resources,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 490560,
    "dDurationMs": 3280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and so our void turns into a battleground."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 493840,
    "dDurationMs": 4720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So which replicator will win? What \nkind of properties will the void favor?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 498560,
    "dDurationMs": 3840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Well, let's try to simulate what happens."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 502400,
    "dDurationMs": 2560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now, if you’re looking to \nrun your own simulations,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 504960,
    "dDurationMs": 2000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "or need a place to run your own code"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 506960,
    "dDurationMs": 2640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "look no further than today’s sponsor — Hostinger."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 509600,
    "dDurationMs": 3360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Say you wanted to keep track \nof everyday science news."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 512960,
    "dDurationMs": 2320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Manually filtering through thousands of articles  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 515280,
    "dDurationMs": 4240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "for the most important stories \nwould be almost impossible!"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 519520,
    "dDurationMs": 2640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But Hostinger lets you easily automate this."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 523040,
    "dDurationMs": 4080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You can use n8n, a platform \nthat lets you automate tasks,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 527120,
    "dDurationMs": 1920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but you need a place to host it."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 529040,
    "dDurationMs": 4480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And the easiest, most price-effective and \nsecure place to host n8n workflows is on  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 533520,
    "dDurationMs": 3280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "a Virtual Private Server or VPS from Hostinger!"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 536800,
    "dDurationMs": 3120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It’s like a powerful computer \nyou rent on the cloud."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 539920,
    "dDurationMs": 2480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So here’s how you can create an article scrubber:"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 542400,
    "dDurationMs": 4240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The workflow can grab every new \nscience article from a list of portals."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 546640,
    "dDurationMs": 4240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Then, it can send the articles to \nChat GPT to summarize their content."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 550880,
    "dDurationMs": 3200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And finally, you can add these quick \nsummaries to a board in Notion."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 554080,
    "dDurationMs": 2720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Using Hostinger’s pre-installed n8n template,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 556800,
    "dDurationMs": 4240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the setup only takes one click, and \nyou’re good to start creating workflows."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 561040,
    "dDurationMs": 2720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "By hosting n8n on a Hostinger VPS,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 563760,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you get all the resources needed to \nrun your workflow smoothly, 24/7!"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 568320,
    "dDurationMs": 3280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Plus, you can have unlimited \nworkflows running simultaneously."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 571600,
    "dDurationMs": 4880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Imagine the things you could do and the time \nyou can save with automations on Hostinger."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 576480,
    "dDurationMs": 3920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "They’re having a Black Friday \nsale right now, so don’t miss out!"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 580400,
    "dDurationMs": 4160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Scan this QR code or visit \nhostinger.com/veritasiumn8n  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 584560,
    "dDurationMs": 4480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and use the code VERITASIUM to get an \nextra discount on top of the sale prices!"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 589040,
    "dDurationMs": 5360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Thanks to Hostinger for sponsoring this part \nof the video, and now back to our simulation."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 594400,
    "dDurationMs": 2400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "To simulate what a replicator \nbattle might look like,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 596800,
    "dDurationMs": 4240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "let's assign simplified traits to each of \nthe replicators, starting with the first one."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 601760,
    "dDurationMs": 1440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This replicator is special,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 603200,
    "dDurationMs": 4000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "since it's the only one that can form \nspontaneously from smaller building blocks."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 607200,
    "dDurationMs": 2000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So we'll give it a spawn rate."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 609200,
    "dDurationMs": 1440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This should be quite rare,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 610640,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "so let's set the chance of \nformation to 1% per time step."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 615200,
    "dDurationMs": 4720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Just keep in mind we're just making these numbers \nup. The simulation is purely illustrative."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 619920,
    "dDurationMs": 1840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now, once the replicator spawns,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 621760,
    "dDurationMs": 2480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "let's say it's governed by three key traits."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 624240,
    "dDurationMs": 1200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "First, a death rate,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 625440,
    "dDurationMs": 3680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the chance of it falling apart or \nbeing destroyed with each time step."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 629120,
    "dDurationMs": 2720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Let's set that to be, say, 2%."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 631840,
    "dDurationMs": 1680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Second, a replication rate,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 633520,
    "dDurationMs": 2480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the chance to copy itself with each time step."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 636000,
    "dDurationMs": 1520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Let's say 4%."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 637520,
    "dDurationMs": 2000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And finally, a mutation rate,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 639520,
    "dDurationMs": 2000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the chance a copy comes out mutated."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 641520,
    "dDurationMs": 4880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If it's 4%, roughly one in \n25 copies will be a mutation."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 646400,
    "dDurationMs": 2480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So every time a new mutation spawns,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 648880,
    "dDurationMs": 4240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "it will inherit the replication death \nand mutation stats from its parent,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 653120,
    "dDurationMs": 1840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but slightly randomized."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 654960,
    "dDurationMs": 3440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Notice that we won't give any of these \nsecondary replicators a spawn rate."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 658400,
    "dDurationMs": 3520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "They'll only be able to form as \nmutations from previous generations."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 661920,
    "dDurationMs": 4240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So if all of their copies die \nout, they'll be gone for good."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 666160,
    "dDurationMs": 1360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now, before we run the simulation,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 667520,
    "dDurationMs": 2320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I want to quickly shout out \nthe YouTube channel Primer."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 669840,
    "dDurationMs": 4480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Our setup was inspired by his amazing \nin-depth simulations on evolutionary biology."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 674320,
    "dDurationMs": 1760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You should really check him out."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 676080,
    "dDurationMs": 2080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Okay, let's run it."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 678160,
    "dDurationMs": 2400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The graph on the right will \nshow how the populations grow,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 680560,
    "dDurationMs": 2560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and this box on the left will \nshow a slice of the void,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 683120,
    "dDurationMs": 3200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "with all the winning replicators \nand the correct ratios."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 686960,
    "dDurationMs": 4480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You can see how the first replicator \nappears and then immediately disappears,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 691440,
    "dDurationMs": 3920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "because it just happened to die \nbefore it got the chance to replicate."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 695360,
    "dDurationMs": 800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But that's okay."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 696160,
    "dDurationMs": 5600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The original replicator can be created from \nsmaller blobs, so it'll come back at some point."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 701760,
    "dDurationMs": 2640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This time, it's starting to take off."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 704400,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You can also see that it spawns some \nmutations, but they're struggling to keep up."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 708960,
    "dDurationMs": 5120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Eventually, though, superior mutations pop up \nand start to replicate faster than the original."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 714080,
    "dDurationMs": 4720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But you can see almost all of them are \ngrowing exponentially, which is unrealistic."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 718800,
    "dDurationMs": 2960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That's because we're missing the \nfinal piece of our simulation,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 721760,
    "dDurationMs": 1440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "limited resources."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 723200,
    "dDurationMs": 2640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The building blocks should eventually run out."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 725840,
    "dDurationMs": 2320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "We can simulate this effect by introducing a sort  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 728160,
    "dDurationMs": 3600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of resource factor to each \nspecies' replication rate."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 731760,
    "dDurationMs": 4640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This factor should depend on the total \nnumber of replicators in the void, N,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 736400,
    "dDurationMs": 4160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "which will also divide with an \narbitrary crowding factor, C."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 740560,
    "dDurationMs": 4640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "C lets us define the maximum number of \nreplicators we'll allow into the void."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 745200,
    "dDurationMs": 1760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Say C is 10,000."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 746960,
    "dDurationMs": 2240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Then once there are 10,000 replicators,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 749200,
    "dDurationMs": 4000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the two terms cancel out and drive \nthe replication rate down to zero,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 753200,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "meaning none of the replicators will be able to \nmake copies until the population drops again. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 757760,
    "dDurationMs": 3360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So let's see how this changes our simulation."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 761120,
    "dDurationMs": 480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Okay."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 761600,
    "dDurationMs": 3360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Like the last time, the original \nreplicator starts to grow,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 764960,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "after which it's quickly \ntaken over by its mutations,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 769760,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but this time, most of these mutation \npopulations start to decline."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 774560,
    "dDurationMs": 3280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Because of the scarce resources, \nthe new best population,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 777840,
    "dDurationMs": 1360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the lime one,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 779200,
    "dDurationMs": 3120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "actually starts stealing \nresources from the others."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 782320,
    "dDurationMs": 4480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "After that, a few more mutations pop \nup, even more powerful than the lime."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 786800,
    "dDurationMs": 2640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Ultimately, the purple replicator takes over,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 789440,
    "dDurationMs": 3760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "occupying around 9,000 of \nthe 10,000 available spaces."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 793200,
    "dDurationMs": 3680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It completely curbs all the other populations."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 796880,
    "dDurationMs": 4400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It goes without saying that the environment \nplays a massive role in which replicator wins."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 801280,
    "dDurationMs": 3440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If you change the environment, \nyou likely change the outcome."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 804720,
    "dDurationMs": 4480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But let's look at the stats of the \nreplicator that came out on top this time."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 809200,
    "dDurationMs": 3600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That winning species has \na replication rate of 20%,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 812800,
    "dDurationMs": 3520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "compared to the 17% average \nacross all populations."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 816320,
    "dDurationMs": 3040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Obviously, being able to \nreplicate quickly pays off here."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 819360,
    "dDurationMs": 2000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Its death rate is below average."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 821360,
    "dDurationMs": 3360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Replicators that fall apart less \nquickly can make more copies."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 824720,
    "dDurationMs": 6000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And finally, it has a 1% mutation \nrate, compared to the average of 3.73%."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 830720,
    "dDurationMs": 2960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Although mutations help by injecting diversity,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 833680,
    "dDurationMs": 1520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "for any single species,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 835200,
    "dDurationMs": 2880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "fewer mutations mean more faithful copies."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 838800,
    "dDurationMs": 5360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If we rerun the simulation, you'll notice \nthe outcomes are always slightly different,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 844160,
    "dDurationMs": 6160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but the winning species consistently have high \nreplication and low death and mutation rates."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 850320,
    "dDurationMs": 2480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now, in the real void, things \nwouldn't have been as simple."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 852800,
    "dDurationMs": 1840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Instead of just tweaking these three stats,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 854640,
    "dDurationMs": 4640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the replicators would have to mutate all \nsorts of different ways to gain an advantage."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 859280,
    "dDurationMs": 4640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "For example, one replicator might mutate a \ntrait that lets it destroy other individuals"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 863920,
    "dDurationMs": 3520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and then use their building blocks \nto make more copies of itself."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 867440,
    "dDurationMs": 2000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This looks like strategy,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 869440,
    "dDurationMs": 3440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but it's really just chemistry \nthat gets copied over and over  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 872880,
    "dDurationMs": 2480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "because it helps the replicator survive."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 875360,
    "dDurationMs": 5360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Naturally, a risk of offense would \nlikely favor mutations that result in defense."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 880720,
    "dDurationMs": 2880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So an opposing replicator might \nstumble upon a mutation that helps  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 883600,
    "dDurationMs": 2720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "it form protective barriers from nearby materials,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 886320,
    "dDurationMs": 2640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "letting it endure those attacks."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 888960,
    "dDurationMs": 3920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "These barriers would also help protect the \nfragile replicators from environmental damage,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 892880,
    "dDurationMs": 1760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "like UV light."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 894640,
    "dDurationMs": 1920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This marks an important threshold."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 896560,
    "dDurationMs": 2400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The replicator's traits aren't limited to just  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 898960,
    "dDurationMs": 2720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "determining the properties \nof the molecules themselves."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 901680,
    "dDurationMs": 2400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "They can also shape the environment."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 904080,
    "dDurationMs": 960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So by chance,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 905040,
    "dDurationMs": 4000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the replicators inevitably mutate in \nways that build scaffolding around  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 909040,
    "dDurationMs": 3360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "themselves to increase the \nchances of their survival."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 912400,
    "dDurationMs": 3920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "They stumble upon ways of making \nstructures to propel themselves around."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 916320,
    "dDurationMs": 3040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "They develop senses and ways of storing energy."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 919360,
    "dDurationMs": 3920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "They even mix, exchange, and \nsteal traits from each other."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 923280,
    "dDurationMs": 5680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Through billions of years of trial and error, \nthis scaffolding gets more and more complex,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 928960,
    "dDurationMs": 880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and as a result,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 929840,
    "dDurationMs": 5280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the replicator's interactions with \nthe void become exceedingly indirect."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 935120,
    "dDurationMs": 3120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "They build complex survival \nmachines for themselves,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 938240,
    "dDurationMs": 4640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "machines whose sole purpose is to \nprotect the replicators inside."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 942880,
    "dDurationMs": 3120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "These machines became such experts at surviving,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 946000,
    "dDurationMs": 3440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "they're still around some 4 billion years later."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 949440,
    "dDurationMs": 1760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "They are the bacteria,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 951200,
    "dDurationMs": 640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "plants,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 951840,
    "dDurationMs": 560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "fungi,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 952400,
    "dDurationMs": 2240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and animals all around you."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 954640,
    "dDurationMs": 1520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Everything alive,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 956160,
    "dDurationMs": 1200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "including you,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 957360,
    "dDurationMs": 3840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "was built as a survival \nvessel for these replicators."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 961200,
    "dDurationMs": 3040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But today, you'd barely \nrecognize them as replicators."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 964240,
    "dDurationMs": 4400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now we just call them genes."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 968640,
    "dDurationMs": 3040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "They're hidden deep within every living creature,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 971680,
    "dDurationMs": 4960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "strands of DNA made from the sequences \nof A, T, G, and C nucleotides."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 976640,
    "dDurationMs": 2080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now, one of the leading theories is that those  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 978720,
    "dDurationMs": 3920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "earliest replicators were actually \nsomething closer to RNA molecules,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 982640,
    "dDurationMs": 880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but then over time,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 983520,
    "dDurationMs": 3600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "this must have evolved into a more \nstable system of storing information,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 987120,
    "dDurationMs": 2320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the DNA and proteins we use today."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 989440,
    "dDurationMs": 2480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "They are the code that shapes our traits."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 991920,
    "dDurationMs": 3760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "We’re taught that these traits are \nhere solely to help ensure our survival"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 995680,
    "dDurationMs": 3200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the survival of the individual or the species."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 998880,
    "dDurationMs": 2800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But do we have this the wrong way around?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1001680,
    "dDurationMs": 2800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "When you have a child, what do you \npass on? The DNA. The DNA, the genes."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1004480,
    "dDurationMs": 160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Yeah, the genes.\nGenes."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1004640,
    "dDurationMs": 2240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Okay, yeah."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1006880,
    "dDurationMs": 4880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "These tiny replicators are still fighting the \nsame battle that started billions of years ago,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1011760,
    "dDurationMs": 2000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and the logic behind them hasn't changed."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1013760,
    "dDurationMs": 2480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The traits just become more convoluted."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1016240,
    "dDurationMs": 4320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Replicators that produce traits poorly suited \nto their environment tend to become less common,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1020560,
    "dDurationMs": 4080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "while those that produce advantageous traits \nbecome more numerous in the population."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1024640,
    "dDurationMs": 2880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So it's not about the fittest individual or group,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1027520,
    "dDurationMs": 3280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "it's fundamentally about the \nsurvival of the fittest genes."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1030800,
    "dDurationMs": 3360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "They are the core unit of natural selection."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1034160,
    "dDurationMs": 3360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But why would natural selection \ncare exactly for the gene?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1037520,
    "dDurationMs": 3680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Why not something smaller or something bigger?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1041200,
    "dDurationMs": 1920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Well, for something to undergo selection,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1043120,
    "dDurationMs": 2000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "it needs to have three characteristics."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1045120,
    "dDurationMs": 3520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "First, it needs to be able to make \nnear identical copies of itself."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1048640,
    "dDurationMs": 4880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Second, it needs to exhibit traits that affect \nits interaction with the environment which,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1053520,
    "dDurationMs": 4320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "third, affect the probability of survival \nand reproduction of the replicator."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1057840,
    "dDurationMs": 3440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Something small like a single \nnucleotide doesn't work, because,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1061280,
    "dDurationMs": 2240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "sure, it'll make identical copies of itself,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1063520,
    "dDurationMs": 880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but alone,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1064400,
    "dDurationMs": 3440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "it doesn't exhibit a trait \nthat could be selected for."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1067840,
    "dDurationMs": 2480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "What about something bigger, like a chromosome?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1070320,
    "dDurationMs": 2800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Well, each chromosome affects \npotentially thousands of traits  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1073120,
    "dDurationMs": 1840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that could influence its survival,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1074960,
    "dDurationMs": 1840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but when most creatures reproduce,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1076800,
    "dDurationMs": 2320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "sections of chromosomes get swapped around."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1079120,
    "dDurationMs": 4160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So a chromosome doesn't stay together \nas a cohesive replicating unit,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1083280,
    "dDurationMs": 2800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and therefore it can't be selected for."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1086080,
    "dDurationMs": 2400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But a gene is somewhere in the middle."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1088480,
    "dDurationMs": 4080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It's a long enough stretch of DNA that \nit can independently influence a trait,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1092560,
    "dDurationMs": 5040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but it's also short and stable enough to be \nfaithfully copied over into future generations."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1097600,
    "dDurationMs": 3600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This is why the gene is the \nunit of natural selection."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1101200,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This perspective led to one of the most powerful \nand controversial ways of seeing evolution,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1105760,
    "dDurationMs": 3440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "one popularized by Richard Dawkins \nin his book The Selfish Gene."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1109200,
    "dDurationMs": 3520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Based on the work of evolutionary \nbiologists in the 1960s and 1970s."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1112720,
    "dDurationMs": 2720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And as a response against the, then very popular,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1115440,
    "dDurationMs": 1440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "group selection theory."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1116880,
    "dDurationMs": 2160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Dawkins argued that just about every trait,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1119040,
    "dDurationMs": 3120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "from animals helping each other \nto being completely selfish,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1122160,
    "dDurationMs": 3840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "is a strategy that helps their \ngenes survive and replicate."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1126000,
    "dDurationMs": 3840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Genes that maximize their own survival \nare the genes that propagate best,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1129840,
    "dDurationMs": 2560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "even if they do so at the expense of others."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1132400,
    "dDurationMs": 1680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Or in Dawkins' words,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1134080,
    "dDurationMs": 2080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "we are survival machines,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1136160,
    "dDurationMs": 6720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "robot vehicles blindly programmed to preserve \nthe selfish molecules known as genes."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1142880,
    "dDurationMs": 3440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now, you might think this framework \nisn't all that groundbreaking."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1146320,
    "dDurationMs": 3440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I mean, take the emperor penguins \nin Antarctica for example."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1149760,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "They hesitate to jump into the water until \nthey are sure there are no seals around."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1154320,
    "dDurationMs": 3840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So what kind of genes could help a \npenguin survive in this environment?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1158160,
    "dDurationMs": 2960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Well, if the penguin’s set of genes \nmake it more likely to be timid,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1161120,
    "dDurationMs": 3920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the penguin might stay back until \nsomeone braver tests the water."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1165040,
    "dDurationMs": 2560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That way, the penguin is at \na lower risk of being eaten,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1167600,
    "dDurationMs": 5120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and has a better chance to survive, \nreproduce and pass on its ‘timid’ genes."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1172720,
    "dDurationMs": 3680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Here, you can think about this either \nas ‘the timid genes help the penguin’"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1176400,
    "dDurationMs": 2480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "or ‘the penguin helps the timid genes’."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1178880,
    "dDurationMs": 1280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Either way works."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1180160,
    "dDurationMs": 4160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So is there any real benefit to viewing \nthings from the gene's perspective?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1184320,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Well, look at what happens when you use these \ntwo frameworks to explain altruistic behavior,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1188880,
    "dDurationMs": 2800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "which appears in a lot of places in nature."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1191680,
    "dDurationMs": 2480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Take California ground squirrels for example."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1194160,
    "dDurationMs": 2880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Females will let out alarm \ncalls if they spot a predator,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1197040,
    "dDurationMs": 1680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "like a fox or a hawk,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1198720,
    "dDurationMs": 5280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to warn other nearby squirrels, even \nthough this puts her survival at risk."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1204000,
    "dDurationMs": 4160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The genes influencing this behavior \nsurely don’t help the squirrel."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1208160,
    "dDurationMs": 2800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But can the squirrel still help the genes?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1210960,
    "dDurationMs": 1920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I think this is a bit more \nclear if you think about the  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1212880,
    "dDurationMs": 3120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "fact that most living things reproduce sexually."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1216000,
    "dDurationMs": 640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Right."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1216640,
    "dDurationMs": 4720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So a squirrel will get half its DNA \nfrom its mom and half from its dad."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1221360,
    "dDurationMs": 3120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So it's actually sharing half \nits genes with each parent."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1224480,
    "dDurationMs": 2000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But also, any child that it has,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1226480,
    "dDurationMs": 4640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "it's also going to share half of its genes \nwith the child, but also any siblings."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1231120,
    "dDurationMs": 5760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But then if you take a step out to an uncle or up \nto a grandparent, then it's sharing one-quarter,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1236880,
    "dDurationMs": 2000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and then another step out is one-eighth."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1238880,
    "dDurationMs": 4320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "All to say, you share a lot of \ngenes with your immediate family."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1243200,
    "dDurationMs": 5040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And California ground squirrels, females \nin particular, they live around family."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1248240,
    "dDurationMs": 4240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So if a squirrel has a set of genes that \nmake her call out when it spots a predator,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1252480,
    "dDurationMs": 3200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "there is a very good chance that the \nsquirrels that hear her warning call"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1255680,
    "dDurationMs": 1680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "also carry those genes."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1257360,
    "dDurationMs": 1920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now, as a result of her alarm call,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1259280,
    "dDurationMs": 4720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "let's say the squirrel attracts a predator \nher way, and it ends up getting eaten."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1264000,
    "dDurationMs": 3840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This action cost the ‘call’ genes \nthe chance to pass themselves on  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1267840,
    "dDurationMs": 3040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to any future offspring of that squirrel."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1270880,
    "dDurationMs": 3760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But, if the warning call saved \nat least 2 copies of those genes"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1274640,
    "dDurationMs": 1760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in two of the squirrel’s relatives…"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1276400,
    "dDurationMs": 2720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "well then, in total, these \n2 squirrels have a better"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1279120,
    "dDurationMs": 4640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "chance of passing on the genes through their \noffspring than the single squirrel did."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1283760,
    "dDurationMs": 4000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "From the gene's perspective, \nthis could be a good trade-off."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1287760,
    "dDurationMs": 3120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It doesn’t matter which individual \nhelps the genes replicate,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1290880,
    "dDurationMs": 3280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "only that as many copies as possible survive."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1294160,
    "dDurationMs": 4640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This principle, that altruistically helping your \nclose relatives helps preserve your own genes,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1298800,
    "dDurationMs": 2160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "is known as kin selection."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1300960,
    "dDurationMs": 3520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And the payoff behind any altruistic \ngesture under kin selection"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1304480,
    "dDurationMs": 4000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "depends heavily on how related you \nare to the individuals you're helping,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1308480,
    "dDurationMs": 1840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "because the less related you are,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1310320,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the smaller the chances that you will share \nthat particular gene with another individual."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1314880,
    "dDurationMs": 1840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And you can see this in nature."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1316720,
    "dDurationMs": 7120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Male squirrels that don't live near relatives \nalmost never give out warning calls."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1323840,
    "dDurationMs": 4480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now, there is a big question this \ngene-centric view still has to address."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1328320,
    "dDurationMs": 3040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If selection really favors \ngenes that replicate well,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1331360,
    "dDurationMs": 3200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "then why would sex ever evolve \nas a means of replication,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1334560,
    "dDurationMs": 2720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "if it throws away roughly half the genes?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1337280,
    "dDurationMs": 1920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Most animals reproduce sexually."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1339200,
    "dDurationMs": 2160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So why do it, when some organisms,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1341360,
    "dDurationMs": 1520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "like certain plants and fungi,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1342880,
    "dDurationMs": 3760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "get to pass on all of their genes \nthrough asexual reproduction?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1346640,
    "dDurationMs": 4000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "From a gene's perspective, this \nseems like a much better deal."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1350640,
    "dDurationMs": 3920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "When it comes to sexual \nreproduction, people like to say,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1354560,
    "dDurationMs": 4080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "\"Okay. Well, it mixes up the genes. \nIt's like shuffling a deck of cards,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1358640,
    "dDurationMs": 4237,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and isn't that better for creating more \nvariation? And clearly, that's advantageous.\""
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1363120,
    "dDurationMs": 4640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Another way this has been explained \nis if the genes that regulate sexual  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1367760,
    "dDurationMs": 3840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "reproduction benefit from replicating sexually,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1371600,
    "dDurationMs": 2320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "then they're going to keep \npushing for these genes."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1373920,
    "dDurationMs": 880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Right."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1374800,
    "dDurationMs": 3520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Even if it's a net negative to \nall the other genes in the genome."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1378320,
    "dDurationMs": 720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Yeah."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1379040,
    "dDurationMs": 3040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So if it benefits them, \nthey'll keep pushing for it."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1382080,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So are there any problems with how The \nSelfish Gene explains natural selection?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1386880,
    "dDurationMs": 5200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Well, yes. I mean, it turns out the \nframework comes with a lot of controversy."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1394240,
    "dDurationMs": 4480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "One of the biggest criticisms against The \nSelfish Gene is that it leaves little to chance."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1398720,
    "dDurationMs": 4400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It implies that every gene present in the genome \nis there because it actively got selected for,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1403120,
    "dDurationMs": 3520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "by natural selection, over many generations."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1406640,
    "dDurationMs": 3120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But many genes are actually \ninvisible to natural selection,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1409760,
    "dDurationMs": 3520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "because they don't really exhibit \nmeaningful traits in the population."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1413280,
    "dDurationMs": 3200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Yet, they can still evolve over time."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1416480,
    "dDurationMs": 2000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Imagine 20 blind cave fish,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1418480,
    "dDurationMs": 2320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "10 with green eyes and 10 with blue."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1420800,
    "dDurationMs": 960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Since they’re blind,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1421760,
    "dDurationMs": 3520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "we’ll assume that their eye color traits \nmake no difference to their survival"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1425280,
    "dDurationMs": 2400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "so they get passed down purely by chance."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1427680,
    "dDurationMs": 1600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now, to form the next generation,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1429280,
    "dDurationMs": 3120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "randomly “pick” any fish from \nthe first group and replicate it."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1432400,
    "dDurationMs": 3200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If you repeat this 20 times, \nyou get a 2nd generation."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1435600,
    "dDurationMs": 4000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "By chance alone, one color will probably \nappear more often than the other."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1439600,
    "dDurationMs": 3600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And if you repeat this \nprocess over many generations,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1443200,
    "dDurationMs": 2880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "one color might eventually completely take over."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1446080,
    "dDurationMs": 1040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Not because it’s better,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1447120,
    "dDurationMs": 2400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but purely due to random sampling."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1449520,
    "dDurationMs": 3680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This shift in the frequency of gene \nvariants is called genetic drift."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1453200,
    "dDurationMs": 2240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It’s most apparent in small populations and for  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1455440,
    "dDurationMs": 2720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "traits that aren't pruned \nfor by natural selection."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1458160,
    "dDurationMs": 3840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But it doesn’t only apply to silent genes."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1462000,
    "dDurationMs": 2000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Even when genes exhibit meaningful traits,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1464000,
    "dDurationMs": 3200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "there is a chance that genetic \ndrift overrides natural selection,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1467200,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and a less fit gene will spread \nthrough the population just by chance."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1471760,
    "dDurationMs": 1600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Look back at our replicator battle."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1473360,
    "dDurationMs": 2000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If we run our simulation enough times,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1475360,
    "dDurationMs": 4400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "sometimes the winning gene won’t be the one \nwith the traits that maximize its own survival."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1479760,
    "dDurationMs": 4160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Here, you can see that the winning population \nactually has a higher than average mutation rate,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1483920,
    "dDurationMs": 1120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "just by chance."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1485040,
    "dDurationMs": 4080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And the average mutation rate is \nalso higher than the starting value."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1489120,
    "dDurationMs": 3600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "These are simplified examples, \nbut there is an ongoing argument  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1492720,
    "dDurationMs": 3520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "about how much of evolution was \nactually due to natural selection"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1496240,
    "dDurationMs": 2880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and how much of it was up to chance."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1499120,
    "dDurationMs": 2800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Another major criticism of \nThe Selfish Gene is about the  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1501920,
    "dDurationMs": 2640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "unavoidable implication behind the word selfish."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1504560,
    "dDurationMs": 2720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It seems to imply that genes have agency,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1507280,
    "dDurationMs": 3840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "like they know what they're doing \nand they understand the consequences,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1511120,
    "dDurationMs": 1600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but it's only a metaphor,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1512720,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "just as portraying them as characters was a \nway for us to make the story more engaging."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1517520,
    "dDurationMs": 3120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Of course, molecules don't \nknow what they're doing."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1520640,
    "dDurationMs": 4720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "They don't decide to replicate or \nconspire to out-compete others."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1525360,
    "dDurationMs": 3360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "They just react according to the laws of physics."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1528720,
    "dDurationMs": 1680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So what may look like intention"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1530400,
    "dDurationMs": 4320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "is just simple chemistry that \nhappens to work well and propagates."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1534720,
    "dDurationMs": 3360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But perhaps the most obvious and \neasiest to understand criticism is  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1538080,
    "dDurationMs": 2640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that the whole framework is an oversimplification,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1540720,
    "dDurationMs": 880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and that's true."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1541600,
    "dDurationMs": 2160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Genes are much more complicated than we thought."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1543760,
    "dDurationMs": 3120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It's not as simple as one gene equals one trait."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1546880,
    "dDurationMs": 4240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "One gene can influence many traits, and \none trait can be influenced by many genes."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1551120,
    "dDurationMs": 3680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "There are genes that are wholly \ncontained within other genes."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1554800,
    "dDurationMs": 2480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "There are genes that inhibit or activate others,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1557280,
    "dDurationMs": 3200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and then there are even genes that \nseem to not encode for anything,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1560480,
    "dDurationMs": 2560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the so-called non-coding DNA."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1563040,
    "dDurationMs": 3280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "All to say, we still have \na lot to learn about genes."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1566320,
    "dDurationMs": 1600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Not to mention that the environment itself,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1567920,
    "dDurationMs": 1120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "like whether it's hot or cold,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1569040,
    "dDurationMs": 1280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "or how much food there is,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1570320,
    "dDurationMs": 2880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "also affects how different genes get expressed."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1573200,
    "dDurationMs": 3600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Genes are much less deterministic \nthan they might seem!"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1576800,
    "dDurationMs": 4000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So you might think that a single gene \nwould rarely have a large enough effect  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1580800,
    "dDurationMs": 2720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that natural selection can directly impact it,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1583520,
    "dDurationMs": 3520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but it doesn't matter how \nconvoluted the pathway is."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1587040,
    "dDurationMs": 3760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If a gene has a measurable effect \non its own survival and replication,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1590800,
    "dDurationMs": 3680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "it will be subject to some \namount of natural selection."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1594480,
    "dDurationMs": 6080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And surely, the whole theory is a simplification, \nbut any theory or framework of nature is."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1600560,
    "dDurationMs": 4320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And what we're covering in this video is an \neven more simplified picture of that framework,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1604880,
    "dDurationMs": 3360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but that doesn't take away the fact \nthat viewing the world through this  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1608240,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "lens has an incredible power to help \nus understand the process of evolution."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1613040,
    "dDurationMs": 4160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It helps us understand why we see such a \nrange of different behaviors in our world"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1617200,
    "dDurationMs": 1200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "because fundamentally,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1618400,
    "dDurationMs": 4720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "those traits tend to cause the increasing \nprevalence of the genes they are associated with."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1623120,
    "dDurationMs": 5280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It's like the whole point \nis figure out what's true."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1628400,
    "dDurationMs": 1040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Get to the truth."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1629440,
    "dDurationMs": 4360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And this, to me, is the \nbaseline truth of evolution."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1633800,
    "dDurationMs": 2520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This is what I love about making Veritasium,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1636320,
    "dDurationMs": 5040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "is that we get to sort of \nunpack and dig under the hood."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1641360,
    "dDurationMs": 3760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And it's what I loved about \nreading The Selfish Gene book,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1645120,
    "dDurationMs": 2160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "is that it really opened my eyes to this."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1647280,
    "dDurationMs": 3760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Previously, I'd always just probably \nthought at the level of the individual,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1651040,
    "dDurationMs": 4880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but it makes more sense to \nthink at the level of the gene."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1655920,
    "dDurationMs": 6320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The feeling that you and every other \nliving organism is being driven by some  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1662240,
    "dDurationMs": 4400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "molecules deep in every cell \nis fundamentally unsettling,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1666640,
    "dDurationMs": 6240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and seems to remove agency from you as \nan acting, thinking being in the world."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1672880,
    "dDurationMs": 2000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Yeah, it's pretty grim."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1674880,
    "dDurationMs": 3440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But whether or not you agree with the fact that  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1678320,
    "dDurationMs": 4640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "we might be controlled by our genes \nand we're simply their flesh robots,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1683600,
    "dDurationMs": 4240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I think it's kind of unreasonable \nand unrealistic to go through life  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1687840,
    "dDurationMs": 2080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "thinking that every decision is governed by this."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1689920,
    "dDurationMs": 1440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It doesn't really do you any good,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1691360,
    "dDurationMs": 2960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "because we perceive the world as individuals."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1694320,
    "dDurationMs": 8320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So I think it's very beneficial to see \nyourself as your own thing, as your own unit."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1705040,
    "dDurationMs": 4160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I want to give a big shout-out to Joe Hanson \nfrom BeSmart for helping us out with this video,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1709200,
    "dDurationMs": 5200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and another shout-out to Primer for letting us \nadapt his simulation on the first replicators."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1714400,
    "dDurationMs": 3120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I have put links to their \nchannels down in the description,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1717520,
    "dDurationMs": 1200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "so please check them out."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1718720,
    "dDurationMs": 2720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And finally, I want to say \na huge shout-out to you."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1721440,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Thank you for watching."
    } ]
  } ]
}
